 Collectors run in several regions and stamp events with their own UTC offset. Legacy collectors (anything installed before 2024) write naive timestamps such as `2024-03-09 22:10:00`; those are UTC. Blank lines are ignored.
 
+To look at recent events only, pass `--since` with a date or ISO 8601 timestamp:
+
+    python -m evlog report events.jsonl --since 2024-03-10
+
+This counts events at or after 00:00 UTC on that day. Timestamps with an offset are converted to UTC before comparing, and naive timestamps are treated as UTC. An unparseable value exits with status 2 and a usage message.
